  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "Circle \\(X\\) has a radius of \\(\\pi.\\) Circle \\(Y\\) has a circumference of \\(8 \\pi.\\) Circle \\(Z\\) has an area of \\(9 \\pi.\\) List the circles in order from smallest to largest radius.",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(X,\\) \\(Y,\\) \\(Z\\)",
    "B": "\\(Z,\\) \\(X,\\) \\(Y\\)",
    "C": "\\(Y,\\) \\(X,\\) \\(Z\\)",
    "D": "\\(Z,\\) \\(Y,\\) \\(X\\)",
    "E": "\\(X,\\) \\(Z,\\) \\(Y\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "First convert the circumference and area into radii so that all three circles can be compared directly. Let \\(r_X,r_Y,r_Z\\) be their positive radii. We are given \\(r_X=\\pi\\).\n\nThe circumference formula \\(C=2\\pi r\\) gives\n\\[\nr_Y=\\frac{8\\pi}{2\\pi}=4.\n\\]\nThe area formula \\(A=\\pi r^2\\) gives \\(r_Z^2=9\\), so \\(r_Z=3\\), because a radius is positive.\n\nUsing \\(\\pi\\approx3.14\\), we have \\(3<\\pi<4\\). Thus the circles in order from smallest to largest radius are \\(Z,X,Y\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
